1
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:12,500
Excuse me, officer.

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:13,800
Can you help me?

3
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:14,700
Sure.

4
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:15,200
Can you tell me

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,200
how to get to Linden Street, in Riverdale?

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,760
Riverdale, New York."

7
00:00:20,760 --> 00:00:22,677
You should take the number 1 subway.

8
00:00:22,677 --> 00:00:23,500
Is there a station near here?

9
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,000
Yes. The station's that way.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,700
You should take the number 1 train

11
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:27,753
to Van Cortlandt Park.

12
00:00:27,753 --> 00:00:30,597
Number 1 train to Van Cortlandt Park. Thank you.

13
00:00:30,597 --> 00:00:31,605
Anytime. Good luck.

14
00:00:31,605 --> 00:00:34,719
Remember, the number 1 train. The uptown platform.

15
00:00:34,719 --> 00:00:36,717
Thank you.

16
00:00:36,717 --> 00:00:51,396
You're welcome.

17
00:00:51,396 --> 00:00:53,718
Is this pink too bright for me?

18
00:00:53,718 --> 00:01:03,100
Mmm-hmm. It is a very bright pink.

19
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:06,993
Try this. It's size eight.

20
00:01:06,993 --> 00:01:09,100
But I wear size ten.

21
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:12,700
How about green? It's size ten.

22
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,354
Let me try it on.

23
00:01:15,354 --> 00:01:20,300
I'm taking too much of your time.

24
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:21,900
It's six o'clock.

25
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:22,900
Where's my husband?

26
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:25,100
I was expecting him here at five forty-five.

27
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:27,300
Don't worry. The traffic is very heavy at this hour.

28
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:31,300
I know. But we're going to be late for dinner.

29
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:32,571
I'll take this green sweater.

30
00:01:32,571 --> 00:01:33,800
I like the color on me, don't you?

31
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:40,900
I think it looks terrific on you.

32
00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:41,500
I'm sorry I'm so late.

33
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:44,496
I had a really bad day.

34
00:01:44,496 --> 00:01:46,800
It's ten after six. We're late.

35
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,600
Robbie's cooking tonight, and dinner's at six thirty.

36
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,900
I know. I know. I'm really sorry.

37
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,172
I left my bag of film on the ferry.

38
00:01:53,172 --> 00:01:55,200
I went back for it, but the ferry was gone.

39
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,000
I lost a whole day's work.

40
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,500
I'll call the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

41
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:07,032
I didn't think of that. Thanks.

42
00:02:07,032 --> 00:02:07,986
Hello.

43
00:02:07,986 --> 00:02:09,900
Yes. The number, please,

44
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:14,300
of the Staten Island Ferry lost-and-found office.

45
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:19,500
Five five five...zero eight zero eight.

46
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,200
Thank you.

47
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,000
I really appreciate it, Marilyn.

48
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,500
Hello.

49
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:29,000
Did anyone find a camera bag this afternoon,

50
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,700
a small canvas bag,

51
00:02:31,700 --> 00:02:38,300
on the J. F. Kennedy Ferry?...No?

52
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,500
Maybe someone will find it.

53
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:42,807
The name is Stewart, Richard Stewart.

54
00:02:42,807 --> 00:02:45,600
And the telephone number is five five five...

55
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:51,500
three oh nine oh. Thank you.

56
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:54,100
Sorry, Richard. They don't have it.

57
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:58,400
Thanks, anyway.

58
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:00,100
There was a girl on the ferry.

59
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:00,924
Now maybe...

60
00:03:00,924 --> 00:03:03,924
Tell me about it on the way home.
